  "brief": "Organigram is acquiring Aurora Cannabis for a reported $561 million, establishing itself as a global cannabis leader.\n\nOrganigram / Aurora Cannabis (Announced): Organigram to Acquire Aurora Cannabis. Organigram is acquiring Aurora Cannabis for a reported $561 million [1, 6, 8]. The deal is expected to establish Organigram as a global cannabis leader [7, 8]. Organigram is outbidding Curaleaf for Aurora Cannabis [8].\nFoodtastic / MTY Food Group (Announced): Foodtastic and MTY Food Group Deal. Foodtastic is a restaurant franchiser that has made a hostile takeover bid for MTY Food Group [12, 13, 14]. MTY Food Group has rebuffed Foodtastic's $720M bid [10]. Foodtastic has offered a $1-billion takeover deal for MTY Food Group [11].\nMarvell Technology / Lumentum Holdings (Announced): Marvell Technology to Acquire Lumentum. Marvell Technology is acquiring Lumentum Holdings in a historic deal [15, 16, 17]. The deal is valued at US$115 billion and is an all-stock transaction [15, 16]. Marvell Technology and Lumentum Holdings have announced the merger agreement [17, 18].\nFox / Roku (Pending approval): Fox to Acquire Roku. Fox is acquiring Roku in a $22 billion cash and stock deal [21, 22, 24]. The deal is pending US antitrust approval [19, 20, 23]. No further updates are available [19, 20, 21].\nArray Technologies / Shoals (Announced): Array Technologies and Shoals Merger Announced. Array Technologies and Shoals are merging [25, 26]. The deal has been announced [25, 26].\nAdkisson / Houston’s Largest Industrial Campus (Announced): Adkisson Lands Houston's Largest Industrial Campus. Adkisson and Houston's Largest Industrial Campus has been announced [27, 28]. No new information is available [27, 28].\nSpectrum Brands / Helen of Troy (Announced): Spectrum Brands Makes Bid on Helen of Troy. Spectrum Brands has made a $37-per-share takeover bid for Helen of Troy [29]. Helen of Troy has rejected the bid [29].\nBrookfield / CPP (Pending approval): Brookfield and CPP Complete LXP Acquisition. Brookfield and CPP have completed the acquisition of LXP Industrial Trust [31, 32, 33]. The acquisition was approved by LXP Industrial Trust shareholders [34, 35]. The deal is pending approval from regulatory bodies [30, 31, 32].\n\nAlso worth knowing:\n- DoorDash is buying Instacart for $17 billion [36].\n- CollPlant Proposes Name Change to OptiPhi Computing After LightSolver Acquisition [37].\n- Is Private Equity Cooked? [38].",
